WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:06.210
Speaker 1: So radical Republican or maybe
confused Republican Senator Lindsey Graham,

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:09.320
Lindsey Graham strikes me more as confused
than radical, I guess, although every once

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.200
in a while he will say something pretty radical.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.640
He suggested assassinating Vladimir Putin,
and then all hell broke loose, and by the

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.789
next day there, there was no more talk of
assassination.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:25.970
Instead, he was talking about arresting Vladimir
Putin, a much more sober and modest suggestion.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:35.650
But I have to tell you what Lindsey Graham
said is not dissimilar to what is going on

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:39.950
in many intelligence agencies back rooms.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.330
It's just you can't publicly say it.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.820
I'm going to explain what I mean.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.870
So let's get to the first clip.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.460
This is Lindsey Graham in the evening.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.400
I think this was Thursday night where he said,
We need a plot.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:57.510
We need someone in there who's going to kill
Putin the way there was a plot to kill Hitler.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:02.980
Speaker 2: How does this in somebody in Russia
has to step up to the plate?

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.930
Is there Brutus in Russia?

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.000
Is there a more successful Colonel Stop Berg
and the Russian military?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.140
The only way this ends, my friend, is for
somebody in Russia to take this guy out.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:18.500
You would be doing your country a great service
and the world a great service right now.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:24.070
Speaker 1: That's that's pretty full on for
for a senator in the United States to say

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.750
the best path is assassinating Putin.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.540
OK, so what is he talking about?

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:34.690
Well, he's talking about Stauffenberg, but
thoughtful name would be Klaus Philip, Maria

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.740
Justinian Schenk, Graf von Stauffenberg.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:48.400
This was a German army officer who I guess
was executed a failed attempt in July of 1944

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.170
to assassinate Adolf Hitler at the so-called
Wolf's Lair.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:57.850
So Lindsay is saying, we need something similar
and we need someone from inside Russia to

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.810
take out Vladimir Putin.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:04.850
So this was completely irresponsible to say.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:06.850
And obviously, it's being considered.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:11.459
I mean, we let's not let's not play dumb here,
guys.

00:02:11.459 --> 00:02:18.999
There is no doubt that every serious intelligence
agency and I'm not defending them from doing

00:02:18.999 --> 00:02:19.999
it.

00:02:19.999 --> 00:02:21.870
I'm just telling you that it's obviously going
on.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:27.599
Every serious intelligence agency is giving
all options to their leaders, and one option

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:29.069
is, could we?

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:32.069
And if so, what would it take?

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:36.870
To assassinate Vladimir Putin or similarly,
I mean, the idea that Lindsey's talking about

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.139
is someone from inside Russia.

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:45.969
Any serious intelligence agency that has moles,
double agents, whatever within Russia would

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:53.010
be saying, Do we have anyone inside of Russia
close enough to Putin that they could potentially

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:54.159
assassinate Putin?

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:57.200
I'm not saying anyone is planning to do it.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.400
I'm not saying that it should be done.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:06.519
I'm saying when you are in a position of providing
options to leadership, you provide every option.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:11.290
And almost always in situations like this,
one of the options is could we kill someone?

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.400
And could we do it with enough plausible deniability
that it can never be traced back to us?

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.049
However, it's not something a senator should
say.

00:03:19.049 --> 00:03:20.049
It's very stupid.

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:24.810
It's extraordinarily dumb for Lindsey Graham
to say it, but to just write it off and pretend

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:28.059
these conversations are being had would be
extraordinarily naive.

00:03:28.059 --> 00:03:31.480
Now, by the next day, Lindsey had completely
backed off.

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.819
Obviously, someone got to him and they were
like that.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:35.849
You can't say that, you can't say that.

00:03:35.849 --> 00:03:39.620
And Lindsey instead said, Well, we should
really be looking at arresting Putin.

